  "body": "## Purpose and scope\n\nRecord the completed Linux x64 implementation and component acceptance for **Task-02: A02, A05, A09, B05, B07, B09, B02, B03 and B06**, with recoverable source identities and the evidence needed to finish normal merge/publication closeout.\n\nCompanion implementation PR: https://github.com/IzuSharp/NativeWeave/pull/13\n\nA01/B01 acceptance is reused from Task-01. The design stays pinned to `c62cdb8aee833b6ab1a03e29a3f59f81a1b483f9`.\n\n## Records delivered\n\n- The batch [handoff](https://github.com/IzuSharp/Plan/blob/task/Task-02-linux/ledger/evidence/batches/Task-02/handoff-linux.md) and [status](https://github.com/IzuSharp/Plan/blob/task/Task-02-linux/ledger/evidence/batches/Task-02/status-linux.json) mark all nine Linux components accepted, identify owners/worktrees/checkpoints and leave merge/publication closeout pending.\n- Task-owned evidence retains source/lock/artifact hashes, full command logs, API/XML checks, actual JIT/NativeAOT execution, independent reviews and resolved findings. Original failed/superseded runs remain distinguishable from final acceptance.\n- B05/B06 acceptance is completed using this batch's real PostgreSQL 18.0 and SQLite 3.51.3 adapters. The provider/stream audit records the exact reviewed source combinations and their scoped follow-ups.\n- All nine implementation branches have final remote checkpoints. The [recovery map](https://github.com/IzuSharp/Plan/blob/task/Task-02-linux/ledger/evidence/batches/Task-02/remote-source-checkpoints-linux.json) records local receipt commits, remote Git Data commits and identical tree hashes; receipts retain the commits that actually ran.\n\n## Principal validation retained\n\n| Area | Evidence |\n| --- | --- |\n| Core and binding contracts — A02/A05/A09 | A02: 84 API/XML symbols, 26 isolated cases and 428 assertions per JIT/AOT mode. A05: JIT 69/AOT 70 assertions and 23 independent probes. A09: JIT 220/AOT 221 assertions, 14 independent probes and six closed findings. |\n| Database components — B05/B07/B09 | B05: 79 symbols, component tests and completed provider acceptance. B07: 120 provider vectors and 4,189 malformed rejections per fixture mode. B09: 42 exact Cdecl declarations, 16 native groups, JIT 66/AOT 67 assertions and separate native/managed reviews. |\n| Providers and streaming — B02/B03/B06 | B02: 11 PostgreSQL groups. B03: 14 SQLite groups. B06: both providers, 598 assertions and 58 cases per JIT/AOT mode, bounded owned resources and zero live cleanup counters. |\n| Combined integration | Six passing commands on clean `c62362d`: Rust formatting/Clippy/Release workspace tests, native assets, locked restore and all **50 solution projects** in Release with zero managed warnings/errors. |\n| Final implementation CI | [43840288797](https://github.com/IzuSharp/NativeWeave/actions/runs/43840288797) passed on remote `25692f957adbf49430b26de8f6b2ece92418e058`. |\n\nScoped CI evidence includes the B09 checker-only formatting correction, the independently accepted SQLite test/docs synchronization repair with 11 focused commands and actual JIT/AOT execution, and narrow Gitleaks false-positive exceptions with independent positive canaries. Production inputs were unchanged by the final formatting/cancellation follow-ups. Failed logs and the SQLite receipt's explicit metadata erratum are preserved.\n\nThe final implementation remote head and local `30c726aab64ab418d40364c8aa5ad9229d68dd78` share tree `155c26f13aa8cfb9ec3af68914e6cd879303f458`. The final Plan checks/review remain the pre-merge gate for this evidence update.\n\n## Closeout and limits\n\nAfter normal merge of both PRs, retain exact merge CI and the existing **HelloWorld-only** preview's final `published-and-consumed` record, verified signature/payload equality and actual registry JIT/AOT results. Record that closeout once.\n\nThe ledger sets Linux implementation/component acceptance complete while keeping batch closeout and global/all-platform acceptance false. Other platforms were not executed; full B04 owning-host composition and pristine component-package consumption remain downstream. This update adds no task package, platform, release package or acceptance standard.\n",
